    apx_tour_load_fail: "🦎 Oops, the tour couldn't load. Try again after a refresh.",
    apx_tour_next: "Next →",
    apx_tour_simple_1: "Welcome home! This is your <b>online ID card</b>. One single link — <b>@you</b> — and you're all set. Follow me, I know every nook (I often hide in them) 🦎",
    apx_tour_simple_2: "Here's your <b>dashboard</b>: your photo, your name, your @. It's your storefront. Put up a nice photo… I won't judge you. Well, barely 😏",
    apx_tour_simple_3: "These switches decide what the world sees: <b>profile, calendar, gallery</b>. You stay in control of everything. Discreet like a chameleon, does that speak to you?",
    apx_tour_simple_4: "The <b>quick actions</b>: your ID, your calendar, your network… and above all <b>Chat</b> and <b>Video call</b>. One click, and there you go.",
    apx_tour_simple_5: "The bottom bar is my remote control: Home, Chat, Network, Calendar, Options… We jump everywhere without getting lost.",
    apx_tour_simple_6: "The <b>messaging</b>! End-to-end encrypted — even I can't read it (and yet, I'm so curious). Pick a contact and dive in.",
    apx_tour_simple_7: "Your <b>detailed card</b>: tags, attributes, photo, QR code. Personalize it all, it's your page and yours alone.",
    apx_tour_simple_8: "And this <b>QR code</b> is your open sesame: scan it, and we're connected. There you go, you know the essentials! Safe travels 🦎",
    apx_tour_tech_1: "Hi, Milo speaking 🦎. <b>Technical</b> version: let's lift the hood. <b>mindlog.talk</b> is a <b>PWA</b> (installable, offline via service worker) that serves as the reference for every client — native Android, Tauri desktop, and the <b>MCP</b> connector.",
    apx_tour_tech_2: "The dashboard is rendered client-side: a <b>vanilla-JS SPA</b>, zero framework. On the other side, the server runs on <b>Hono + Postgres</b> (Drizzle ORM), 100% TypeScript.",
    apx_tour_tech_3: "Every privacy setting is persisted server-side and applied to your public page. Profile, calendar, gallery: <b>flag-level granularity</b>, changed live.",
    apx_tour_tech_4: "Messaging: <b>E2E encryption via Double Ratchet</b>, session setup through <b>X3DH</b> (custom P-256). The server only stores ciphertext — <b>forward secrecy</b> included. Even I only see gibberish.",
    apx_tour_tech_5: "The <b>key vault</b>: your private key is encrypted <i>inside</i> the browser (passkey PRF or passphrase) then stored unreadable. The server never sees the key in the clear — nor your passphrase.",
    apx_tour_tech_6: "<b>Signal-style multi-device</b>: each device has its own key, envelopes are broadcast via <b>fan-out</b>, and a new device must be <b>approved</b> from an already-active device.",
    apx_tour_tech_7: "A <b>3-degree</b> network, anti-MITM verification via <b>safety number</b> (QR to scan). And groups? <b>Sender keys</b> + ECDSA signatures. Serious stuff.",
    apx_tour_tech_8: "Your card is structured: typed attributes, tags, client-side resized photo. All exposed by a <b>documented REST API</b> (OpenAPI).",
